{
  "id": "leetcode-312",
  "version": 1,
  "status": "approved",
  "title": "Burst Balloons",
  "summary": "Given n balloons indexed from 0 to n-1, each with a number on it.",
  "statement": "Given n balloons indexed from 0 to n-1, each with a number on it. Bursting the i-th balloon yields coins equal to nums[i-1] * nums[i] * nums[i+1]. If i-1 or i+1 is out of bounds, consider a balloon with a 1. Find the maximum coins by bursting the balloons optimally.",
  "constraints": [
    "1 <= len(nums) <= 300; 0 <= nums[i] <= 100.",
    "Burst every balloon. Its neighbors are the nearest balloons STILL PRESENT; a missing neighbor has value 1. Return the maximum total coins."
  ],
  "topics": [
    "dynamic-programming",
    "intervals",
    "recursion"
  ],
  "prerequisites": [
    "dynamic-programming",
    "recursion"
  ],
  "signature": {
    "name": "max_burst_coins",
    "parameters": [
      {
        "name": "nums",
        "annotation": "list[int]",
        "adapter": "raw",
        "source_parameter": null
      }
    ],
    "returns": "int",
    "return_adapter": "raw",
    "node_policy": "values",
    "result_mode": "return",
    "mutated_parameter": null,
    "immutable_parameters": []
  },
  "starter_code": "def max_burst_coins(nums: list[int]) -> int:\n    # Write your solution here.\n    pass\n",
  "reference_solution": "def max_burst_coins(nums):\n    values = [1] + nums + [1]\n    size = len(values)\n    dp = [[0] * size for _ in range(size)]\n    for width in range(2, size):\n        for left in range(size - width):\n            right = left + width\n            best = 0\n            boundary = values[left] * values[right]\n            for last in range(left + 1, right):\n                best = max(best, dp[left][last] + dp[last][right] + boundary * values[last])\n            dp[left][right] = best\n    return dp[0][-1]\n",
  "brute_force_solution": null,
  "known_wrong_solutions": [
    "def max_burst_coins(nums):\n    remaining = [1] + nums + [1]\n    total = 0\n    while len(remaining) > 2:\n        i = max(range(1, len(remaining)-1),\n                key=lambda j: remaining[j-1] * remaining[j] * remaining[j+1])\n        total += remaining[i-1] * remaining[i] * remaining[i+1]\n        remaining.pop(i)\n    return total\n",
    "def max_burst_coins(nums):\n    values = [1] + nums + [1]\n    return sum(values[i-1] * values[i] * values[i+1] for i in range(1, len(values)-1))\n"
  ],
  "target_time_complexity": "O(n^3)",
  "target_space_complexity": "O(n^2)",
  "estimated_minutes": 50,
  "rubric": {
    "algorithmic_insight": 3,
    "prerequisites": 2,
    "implementation": 1,
    "performance_pressure": 1,
    "edge_cases": 1
  },
  "hints": [
    "Think about which balloon is removed last within an interval.",
    "The last balloon has fixed outer neighbors, separating the remaining choices into two independent intervals.",
    "Pad with 1s. For each open interval (l,r), maximize dp[l][k]+dp[k][r]+a[l]*a[k]*a[r] over l<k<r.",
    "Fill intervals by increasing width. Empty intervals earn zero; the full padded interval gives the answer."
  ],
  "editorial": "Choosing the first burst changes neighboring subproblems. Choosing the last burst k between fixed boundaries l and r avoids that dependency: every earlier burst lies entirely on one side. Maximize the sum of the two optimal open intervals and the last reward. Increasing interval width provides all dependencies. The oracle independently enumerates first-burst choices on shrinking tuples with memoization.",
